IDENTITY GRAPH

Site spine: UPRN CONFIRMED where source supplies it; otherwise
normalized address + postcode + geometry as INFERRED candidate, never
silently promoted. Preserve source address strings.

Road spine: USRN + geometry + Street Manager
work_reference_number/version. USRN is spatial identity;
work_reference_number is intervention identity.

Bus spine: operator/service + dated vehicle journey reference +
vehicle reference + timetable version. Exposure to roadworks is
INFERRED unless an authoritative route/geometry relationship exists.

Company/provider spine: Companies House number where resolved; scheme
IDs (MCS/OZEV/NICEIC/NAPIT etc.) remain source-native aliases linked
with provenance and validity windows. Never key solely by company
name.

Part spine: manufacturer + MPN + revision/supersession edge. A
compatible substitute is a directed, validity-scoped edge, not
identity equality.

Project spine: authoritative project ID/reference first; owner/company
and connection point are time-varying attributes. Name changes and
ownership transfers create events, not new projects unless
authoritative IDs change.

Every edge must store from_id, to_id, edge_type, valid_from, valid_to,
observed_at, status CONFIRMED|INFERRED|UNKNOWN, confidence,
provenance[], resolver_version and evidence_hash.

EXACT SOURCE STACK

Street Manager: DfT public roadworks API, registration required,
OGL/free. Official guidance:
https://www.gov.uk/guidance/find-and-use-roadworks-data . Public
fields include event_reference, event_type, work_reference_number,
permit_reference_number, promoter/highway authority, coordinates,
work_category, traffic_management_type, proposed/actual start/end,
status, USRN, event_time, object_reference and version. Cadence: live.
Canonical intervention key: work_reference_number + version; event key
event_reference.

Street Manager API Notifications: official docs at
https://department-for-transport-streetmanager.github.io/street-manager-doc=
s/api-notifications/
. Near-real-time semantic events, but authenticated POST
/api-notifications/subscribe is organisation-scoped. Do not assume
this is the national public subscription path.

BODS archive: https://data.datalibrary.uk/transport/BODS-ARCHIVE/sirivm/
. OGL; one request/second; daily downloads containing snapshots saved
about every 30 seconds; 2.74 TB current SIRI-VM archive. Use archive
first, live collection only for gaps or experiments.

EPC: official England/Wales address-level open data; CSV monthly,
developer API daily. Canonical site key UPRN when present;
certificate/lodgement identity preserved separately. Official 2026
statistics note duplicate certificates and daily API updates.

Planning Data planning-application-log:
https://www.planning.data.gov.uk/dataset/planning-application-log .
OGL. Current state remains 0 records, no providers, no collector
attempt. Schema already contains planning-application, status,
event-date, organisation, reference and lifecycle statuses including
submission, document check, missing-document request, consultation and
appeal. This remains a clean t=3D0 trigger.

MCS: installation/certificate data is operationally useful, but public
row-level access and permission path for a broad POW collector remain
unresolved. Treat as PILOT/PERMISSION, not open-data fact.

